# Mobile app rules

The app is a thin client over the engine + Supabase. Routing is Expo Router. State is Zustand. Animations are Reanimated 4 (with the `react-native-worklets` split-out package).

## Hard rules

- **No game logic in components.** If a component contains conditions about cards, turns, or scoring, that logic belongs in the engine or a selector.
- **Components read state via Zustand selectors**, never the full store. Bad: `useStore()`. Good: `useStore((s) => s.myHand)`.
- **All user-visible strings go through `t()`.** Even though we're English-only in v1.
- **No hardcoded colors, spacings, or radii.** Use design tokens from `apps/mobile/src/design/tokens.ts`.
- **Optimistic UI** for moves: dispatch locally via engine, then reconcile on server confirm. If the server rejects, animate back.
- **Reanimated worklets** for anything that runs every frame (card drag, flip). Don't compute derived animation values on the JS thread.

## Folder layout

```
apps/mobile/
├── app/                      # Expo Router routes
│   ├── (auth)/               # sign-in flow
│   ├── (lobby)/              # rooms list, create/join
│   └── (game)/[roomId]/      # active game screen
├── src/
│   ├── components/           # presentational only
│   ├── design/               # tokens, theme, primitives
│   ├── i18n/                 # locales + t() wrapper
│   ├── store/                # Zustand stores + selectors
│   ├── supabase/             # client wrapper, realtime hooks
│   └── engine/               # re-exports from @pablo/engine for convenience
└── assets/
```

## Example: a card component

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — game logic in a component
export function CardSlot({ slotIndex }: { slotIndex: number }) {
  const state = useStore((s) => s.state);
  const isMyTurn = state.players[state.turnIndex] === state.self;
  const canSwap = state.drawn && isMyTurn;
  // ...
}

// ✅ GOOD — read derived flags from selectors
export function CardSlot({ slotIndex }: { slotIndex: number }) {
  const canSwap = useStore(selectCanSwapInto(slotIndex));
  const card = useStore(selectMyCard(slotIndex));
  return <Card card={card} interactive={canSwap} />;
}
```
